      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "5ada6a2bddd9d8099bfc12a8",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Currently, you press the dance emote, your character will do it once, and then stop. Simply put, adding a small box to the bottom left corner of an Emote button that can be toggled to set that particular emote to LOOP until you move, would be a welcome addition. Some emotes however like the DIE animation, may require a different button, perhaps a toggling the button again can set the emote to a STAY mode that grabs the last frame of the animation and holds you in that position until you move would also be good.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Loop Toggle for Emotes",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "59e7986148b4da48e00baf9d",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "_id": "5ada6a41ddd9d8099bfc12ab",
      "author": {
        "_id": "58db230764d6ff1cf2c451c7",
        "alias": "Remaining Marmoset",
        "aliasID": "65ba0196ed6eefce4cf5a714",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/7613c165fbefd0763b0d5dfd092eaae4.jpg",
        "created": "2017-03-29T02:59:19.417Z",
        "name": "Aev",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2018-04-20T22:31:29.679Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "5ada6a41ddd9d8099bfc12ab",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I, among a few others have multiple avatars for different looks on a certain avatar. This leads to really quickly overloading our avatar lists and increasing the chance of running into the inevitable Avatar ID issue that people run into sometimes. \n\nA possible remedy to this issue is that you could have a set of toggle-able emotes that replace something like the Idle animation until you turn it off. this could be VERY, and I mean VERY useful in decreasing the amount of duplicate avatars who have different texts or screens or weapons, ect and compress all that into a single avatar. This would not only help clear up the amount of duplicate avatars, it could also open up a creative tool to be used In ways I couldn't think of right now. \n\nJust as a quick example, this could help decrease the amount of avatar switching I do for my security bot just for different screens and could open up to a more dynamic use of the screens. Not only that but it could help with my up coming Wall-e and Wall-a models as well as help with my Eve model. Allowing me to toggle to position of my arms on wall-e, or turn on or off the plant light on my Eve. I know a few people who would also benefit from a system like this, like having hats you can switch between by have two idles that have 1 hat scaled down and another with it scaled up. People could also have weapons they can switch between, there could be a lot of potential behind this.\n\nPlease check out my other Feature Request \"Longer than 10 second emotes\" :)",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Toggle-able Idle Animations or Emotes",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "59e7986148b4da48e00baf9d",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    },
